   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "How much?",
   "texto": [
    "**Combien de** is for everything, whether or not it is counted: **combien d'œufs ?**, **combien de riz ?**",
    "To express a non-specific amount, **de** (or **d'** before vocal) is used, usually without article: **beaucoup de** (much), **un peu de** (a little), **trop de** (too much), **un kilo de**, **un litre de**.",
    "**Beaucoup de fruits** = many unspecified fruits. **Beaucoup des fruits du panier** can mean «many of the fruits of the basket» if it refers to a specific group."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "It's necessary.",
   "texto": [
    "**Il faut** + name = needed, needed: **Il faut des œufs** (required eggs). It is impersonal and is conjugated in third person singular, even if the name is plural.",
    "**Acheter** is «buy»: **j'achète**, **on achète**.",
    "**Faire les courses** = make the purchase."
   ]
